## CsrBidirectional

Round 202605111719 introduces `CsrBidirectional<ROWS, NNZ, W>` as a
bidirectional CSR wrapping the original adjacency plus its transpose
for O(out_degree) predecessor lookup. The type is documented in
`DESIGN.md.tmpl` under its own section, with the constructor
`Csr::with_transpose(...)` and the `BidirectionalSparseAdjacency`
trait impl. Source landing happens in the round's src CL alongside
the `SparseAdjacency` / `BidirectionalSparseAdjacency` trait family
implementations. Until then, this SHAME entry silences the
push-gate lint while the round is in DOC phase. The entry is
removed when the src CL lands and source matches docs.
